                        "glosses": [
                            "One who lauds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c17e3067-21f9-438b-9f13-f19e64a080d0",
                                "sense_id": "bdba1d46-2f83-3e03-8043-362a22af53b5",
                                "text": "As in most speeches, exaggeration and embellishment were standard devices by which the laudator amplified his subject's virtues or vices."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a5accdc-8b5e-48f8-bc9a-faea631e72d9",
                                "sense_id": "bdba1d46-2f83-3e03-8043-362a22af53b5",
                                "text": "To the extent that he is visible at all, the poet fulfils the role of laudator, not commentator on or representative of a world view."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89d1d30f-a5b6-4d4e-80be-e2a5f035144f",
                                "sense_id": "bdba1d46-2f83-3e03-8043-362a22af53b5",
                                "text": "When he made all those wrong decisions in his business and private life, he expected me to be a sycophant, a laudator,or a yes-man."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
